 OnKeyDown←{
     ⍝ On keydown in body, for menubar
     d←⍵.Document
     0<≢d GetElementsByClass'DialogBox':0
     k←⍵.Code
     b←⍵.(CtrlKey ShiftKey AltKey)∊⊂⊂'true'
     p←k,⍨∊b/'Ctrl' 'Shift' 'Alt'
     ⍵.FQK←p
     FocusMenuBar ⍵:0
     _←OnKeyDownGlobal ⍵
     ⍝ ↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓↓
     ⍝ It's not clear we should do this.
     ⍝ Perhaps we should just report in the event
     ⍝ message that a menu was open, and/or that the menubar was
     ⍝ Active. BETTER YET, Let's just return the Target element
     ⍝ The calling app can then decide to ignore and Escape key, etc.
     0<≢d GetElementsByClass'menu':0
     ⍝ 'MenuBar'≡⍵.Target.class:0
     ⍝ ↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑↑
     e←⎕NS''
     e.Event←'KeyDown'
     e.Target←⍵.Target
     e.Component←d
     e.Key←⍵.FQK
     FireAbacusEvent e
 }
